{#
  module/SionModel/view/sion-model/sion-model/data-problems.phtml, ported.

  Only the **read-only** route moves. That .phtml serves two laminas routes:
  `sion-model/data-problems` (a plain list) and `sion-model/auto-fix-data-problems`,
  which sets `isSimulation` and renders a CSRF-protected confirm form. The auto-fix
  route stays on laminas — there is no form layer on the Symfony side — so the
  simulation branch is deliberately absent here rather than half-reproduced. Under
  PhpRenderer the unset `$this->form` was silently null; under Twig's strict_variables
  it would be an exception, which is a good reason for the branch to be gone rather than
  guarded.

  The entity cell goes through the dispatcher macro rather than format_entity()
  directly: `problem_specifications` names association and person as well as book,
  collection and library, and laminas formats those two with helpers reproduced as
  macros. See templates/schoenstatt/_entity-format.html.twig.

  `displayEditPencil: true` is what the .phtml passes, and it is the default anyway;
  passed explicitly so the two files read the same.
#}
{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{% import 'schoenstatt/_entity-format.html.twig' as fmt %}

{% block content %}
<p><strong>{{ translate('Total problems') }}:</strong>&nbsp;{{ problems|length }}</p>
<table class="table">
	<thead>
	<tr>
	<th>{{ translate('Entity') }}</th>
	<th>{{ translate('Problem') }}</th>
	</tr>
	</thead>
	<tbody>
{% for problem in problems %}
<tr>
	<td>{{ fmt.entity(problem.entity, problem.data, {'displayEditPencil': true}) }}</td>
	<td class="{{ problem.problemTextClass }}">{{ translate(problem.problemText, problem.translatorTextDomain) }}</td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
	</tbody>
</table>
{% endblock %}
